  "text": "Allergies:\nOxazepam\n\nChief Complaint:\nCentral retinal artery occlusion\n\nHistory of Present Illness:\n___ with CKD5 from preeclampsia, ___ miscarriages with no live\nbirths, HTN, HLD who woke in her normal state of health then\naround ___ noticed that the vision in her left eye only was\nbecoming hazy. Within 2 hours, she had complete blindness of the\nleft eye which was totally painless. She states that over the\nlast several years she has had the sensation of haziness in her\nleft eye in the past but usually it passes in a minute or two\nwhen she has some juice.  She thinks it has happened about once\nevery six months and it has never progressed to complete\nblindness before. She denies scalp tenderness or jaw\nclaudication. Of note, she has CKD5 from focal \nglomerulosclerosis\nafter an episode pre-eclampsia in ___. She has had ___\nmiscarriages in the past but was never able to carry a child to\nterm. Her mother died at ___ from kidney failure in childbirth.\nThe patient denies any history of abnormal bruising, bleeding\nfrom the nose or gums, phlebitis. Her menstruations were always\nnormal (not too heavy or light). She thinks she was worked up in\nthe past for bleeding issues but was never placed on any blood\nthinner including Coumadin or aspirin. Ophthalmology was\nconsulted to evaluated the patient in the ED and she was found \nto\nhave an acute CRAO. Neurology was consulted for further workup\nrecommendations. \n\nOn neuro ROS, (+) left eye blindness, she thinks is slightly\nimproved today as she can see some light and movement with the\nleft eye while before it was totally blind. The pt denies\nheadache, diplopia, dysarthria, dysphagia, lightheadedness,\nvertigo, tinnitus or hearing difficulty. Denies difficulties\nproducing or comprehending speech.  Denies focal weakness,\nnumbness, parasthesiae. No bowel or bladder incontinence or\nretention. Denies difficulty with gait.\n \nOn general review of systems, (+) chronic urinary frequency. The\npt denies recent illnesses. Denies cough, shortness of breath. \nDenies chest pain or tightness, palpitations.  Denies nausea,\nvomiting, diarrhea, constipation or abdominal pain.  No recent\nchange in bowel or bladder habits.  No dysuria.  Denies\narthralgias or myalgias. Denies rash.\n\nBrief Hospital Course:\n___ with CKD5 from preeclampsia, ___ miscarriages with no live \nbirths, HTN, HLD who had the onset of left eye haziness which \nprogressed to total blindness in about 2 hours found to have \nleft eye acute CRAO.\n\n#CRAO: Patient presented with a history of painless L visual \nloss on the day of admission. In the ED, she was evaluated by \nophthalmology and found to have CRAO. Admission exam was notable \nfor vision intact to finger movement 10 inches away with best \nvision in the superior temporal quadrant, no distance vision, \nand L afferent pupillary defect. MRI brain showed a small left \nposterior frontal subacute subcortical infarct, and MRA \nbilateral intracranial carotid artery stenosis. Follow-up \ncarotid ultrasound demonstrated <40% stenosis of the R ICA and \n40-59% stenosis of the L ICA. CRAO was felt to be most likely \nsecondary to carotid artery atherosclerosis given that she also \nhad subacute cerebral infarcts. Patient was admitted to the \nStroke Service for work-up and management. Home pravastatin dose \nwas increased from 20 to 40 mg qd and ASA 81 was started. Home \namlodipine 7.5 mg qd was held and home metoprolol 25 mg bid was \nhalved on admission for permissive hypertension. Home doses of \nboth agents were resumed prior to discharge given no evidence \nfor acute infarct on imaging. Stroke risk factors including A1C, \nLDL-C and TSH were checked and were all within normal limits. \nInflammatory markers were found to be elevated (ESR 62, CRP 7). \nA hypercoagulability panel was sent given history of \nmiscarriages; ___ titer, anti-cardiolipin antibody, and \nbeta-2-glycoprotein antibody were pending at the time of \ndischarge. Patient's visual exam remained stable at the time of \ndischarge with sensitivity to light and movement in the left \neye. She was discharged home on ASA 81 mg qd (with plan for 3 \nmonth course followed by lifelong therapy in the absence of \ncontraindication to anticoagulation), Plavix 75 mg qd (with plan \nfor 3 month course), pravastatin 40 mg qd, amlodipine 7.5 mg qd, \nand metoprolol 25 mg bid. TTE was recommended as outpatient to \nrule out cardioembolic etiology of infarct. She had elevated \ninflammatory markers, but these were not as high as is typically \nseen in ___; in addition, GCA would rarely cause an \nintraparenchymal infarct, so this was thought to be unlikely. \nShe will follow up with PCP, ophthalmology (Dr. ___ and \nneurology (Dr. ___.\n\n#Stage V CKD ___ FSGS: Creatinine on admission 4.8 (at \nbaseline). Creatinine and electrolytes remained within normal \nlimits this admission.\n\n#Troponinemia: Troponin on admission elevated to 0.02; less than \nassay on re-check. Attributed to impaired clearance in the \nsetting of CKD.   \n\nAHA/ASA Core Measures for Ischemic Stroke and Transient Ischemic \nAttack  \n1. Dysphagia screening before any PO intake? (x) Yes, confirmed \ndone - () Not confirmed  () No  \n2. DVT Prophylaxis administered? (x) Yes - () No  \n3. Antithrombotic therapy administered by end of hospital day 2? \n(x) Yes - () No  \n4. LDL documented? (x) Yes (LDL = 79) - () No  \n5. Intensive statin therapy administered? (simvastatin 80mg, \nsimvastatin 80mg/ezetemibe 10mg, atorvastatin 40mg or 80 mg, \nrosuvastatin 20mg or 40mg, for LDL > 100) () Yes - (x) No [if \nLDL >100, reason not given: ]  \n6. Smoking cessation counseling given? () Yes - (x) No [reason \n() non-smoker - () unable to participate]  \n7. Stroke education (personal modifiable risk factors, how to \nactivate EMS for stroke, stroke warning signs and symptoms, \nprescribed medications, need for followup) given (verbally or \nwritten)? (x) Yes - () No  \n8. Assessment for rehabilitation or rehab services considered? \n(x) Yes - () No  \n9. Discharged on statin therapy? (x) Yes - () No [if LDL >100, \nreason not given: ]  \n10. Discharged on antithrombotic therapy? (x) Yes [Type: (x) \nAntiplatelet - () Anticoagulation] - () No  \n11. Discharged on oral anticoagulation for patients with atrial \nfibrillation/flutter? () Yes - () No - (x) N/A\n\nDischarge Diagnosis:\nCentral retinal artery occlusion",
